(2156817, 292830, 38032, '<td valign="top">Didn''t get to vote on this one but I definitely would have given you accolades ... similar to the following:<br/> <br/>I can always appreciate extra effort that involves more than just a studio type set-up.  In fact, the non-studio looking setting here brings comfort and makes something that looks real as well as nostalgic.  I think the reason people generally don''t like the usual cat image is that it indicates that someone just pointed-and-shot ... their cat.  This is a great interaction and plan with which you succeeded.  Congrats - this is more inspirational than the DQ''d image.</td>', 'Didn''t get to vote on this one but I definitely would have given you accolades ... similar to the following: I can always appreciate extra effort that involves more than just a studio type set-up.  In fact, the non-studio looking setting here brings comfort and makes something that looks real as well as nostalgic.  I think the reason people generally don''t like the usual cat image is that it indicates that someone just pointed-and-shot ... their cat.  This is a great interaction and plan with which you succeeded.  Congrats - this is more inspirational than the DQ''d image.', '2006-02-16 13:41:09.000000', NULL, 0),
