(2303361, 292135, 28710, '<td valign="top">What a totally sweet picture! The lighting makes this claustrophobic, like it''s in a narrow tunnel or something (?), and highlights the details in the wall while at the same time providing a mood. Other technical details are spot on.<br/> <br/>I didn''t vote in this challenge, but I still think this picture rocks.<br/> <br/>I will honestly say though that I might have missed the doorknob thing... I don''t think it''s legal to draw a big arrow in Red or Yellow saying NO DOORKNOB HERE! SEE? in challenge photos...<br/> <br/>On further inspection, I did notice that there only appears to be one hinge too.<br/>Oh well, it still kicks.<br/> <br/>I personally have a thing for weird doors though.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-11 09:53:50.</i></td>', 'What a totally sweet picture! The lighting makes this claustrophobic, like it''s in a narrow tunnel or something (?), and highlights the details in the wall while at the same time providing a mood. Other technical details are spot on. I didn''t vote in this challenge, but I still think this picture rocks. I will honestly say though that I might have missed the doorknob thing... I don''t think it''s legal to draw a big arrow in Red or Yellow saying NO DOORKNOB HERE! SEE? in challenge photos... On further inspection, I did notice that there only appears to be one hinge too.Oh well, it still kicks. I personally have a thing for weird doors though.', '2006-04-11 10:52:20.000000', '2006-04-11 10:53:50.000000', 0),
(2318448, 290540, 36499, '<td valign="top">just my opinion again.....I think the narow focus is what really hurt this one. the shallow focus actually takes away from the interest factor of this image making the viewer see only the one spot(splinter) I think this wouldve done better with a wider focus, giving the viewer''s eyes room to roam and settle on several different spots in the image. This also lacks a good "pop" of color which DPC is so very fond of. Your colors are spot on( as they look natural to me) and I think the crop is good.</td>', 'just my opinion again.....I think the narow focus is what really hurt this one. the shallow focus actually takes away from the interest factor of this image making the viewer see only the one spot(splinter) I think this wouldve done better with a wider focus, giving the viewer''s eyes room to roam and settle on several different spots in the image. This also lacks a good "pop" of color which DPC is so very fond of. Your colors are spot on( as they look natural to me) and I think the crop is good.', '2006-04-17 09:55:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2318461, 290540, 23394, '<td valign="top">dof makes this a bit too abstract.  the lighting on the right is a bit too strong.  as an entry, this comes across as though you found something broken and zoomed in on it.  you got to close to it for the viewer to get anything from it that would keep their attention.<br/> <br/>as a side note, challenge entries are not counted towards your portfolio space, you should be submitting entries as large as possible, at least 640px on the longest side (this is 550), and as close to 150kb as possible.</td>', 'dof makes this a bit too abstract.  the lighting on the right is a bit too strong.  as an entry, this comes across as though you found something broken and zoomed in on it.  you got to close to it for the viewer to get anything from it that would keep their attention. as a side note, challenge entries are not counted towards your portfolio space, you should be submitting entries as large as possible, at least 640px on the longest side (this is 550), and as close to 150kb as possible.', '2006-04-17 10:01:51.000000', NULL, 0),
